 "questdb_heap_verdict": {
  "verdict": "adequate",
  "chosen_heap": "-Xms1g -Xmx1g",
  "tested_at_that_value": true,
  "default_heap_tested": false,
  "why": "A full day ran to WAL fully applied in class B and again in class A, with no collection at all after start-up. The only pauses are the three full collections every server start makes, 2 for metadata and 1 System.gc(), under 0.25 s in total. The most used after any collection was 116 MiB, and at the end of ingest at most 300 MiB of 982 MiB was in use, with eden never filled. No OutOfMemoryError, no memory pressure, no suspension, no error line. The evidence gives no reason to test another heap.",
  "phase_3_setting": "-Xms1g -Xmx1g for QuestDB on the Linux host, with the launcher's AlwaysPreTouch and ParallelGC",
  "risk": "Neither the heap nor mapped pages. The server's resident mapped pages stayed under 200 MiB during ingest and near 1.1 GiB during queries, and its VmHWM peaked at 2.4 GiB. Most of the lowest MemAvailable comes from the Python ingest client, not the server",
  "client": "The client's anonymous memory climbs about 300 MiB per 4 Mi-row chunk to a ceiling near 5.4 GiB, then falls, and repeats. Arrow's pool stayed under 514 MiB, so the rest is held outside Arrow, by the client's native side. It does not grow with the day: the first peak came at about a quarter of the rows, and later ones were no higher."
 }
